@page "/contact"

<PageTitle>Contact · louis-agent</PageTitle>

<section class="band">
    <span class="kicker">Early access</span>
    <h2 class="chrome">Building an agent for a .NET team?</h2>
    <p class="lede">The engine and its packs are heading for NuGet. Tell us what you're building and we'll show you where it stands, what's measured and what's still to come.</p>
    <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="panel">
            <h3>Write to us</h3>
            <p>One mail, in your own words: what the agent should do, which model you'd run it on, and where it would run.</p>
            <a class="btn btn-fill" href="mailto:[YOUR EMAIL]">Send a mail</a>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
            <h3>Read first</h3>
            <p>The architecture, every design decision and the learning write-ups are public, so you can read why it's built this way before you write.</p>
            <a class="btn btn-line" href="https://github.com/bosbevk/louis-agent">The repository</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
